WEBVTT

1
00:00:28.583 --> 00:00:31.708
In the previous verses of Chapter 16,

2
00:00:31.708 --> 00:00:32.583
Lord Krishna

3
00:00:32.583 --> 00:00:35.291
described the consequences of
demoniac nature.

4
00:00:35.291 --> 00:00:36.500
In verse 16.21

5
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:38.375
He moves beyond description

6
00:00:38.375 --> 00:00:40.791
and now gives a clear directive.

7
00:00:40.791 --> 00:00:43.875
He gives the seeker a direct message.

8
00:00:43.875 --> 00:00:46.875
There are three gateways to hell – kama,

9
00:00:46.875 --> 00:00:49.750
krodha, and lobha.

10
00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:50.833
All three pull the soul

11
00:00:50.833 --> 00:00:53.958
toward degradation.

12
00:00:53.958 --> 00:00:57.750
The purpose of this verse is not to create fear,

13
00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:01.125
but to show the seeker a clear path.

14
00:01:01.125 --> 00:01:03.500
If spiritual progress is desired,

15
00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.833
these three tendencies must be 
turned away from.

16
00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:13.375
Lord Krishna says –

17
00:01:13.375 --> 00:01:16.000
there are three dvaram, gateways, to hell:

18
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.500
kamah, krodhah, and lobhah.

19
00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:22.458
Therefore they must be renounced.

20
00:01:22.458 --> 00:01:24.708
Dvaram is a metaphor.

21
00:01:24.708 --> 00:01:26.333
Just as one enters

22
00:01:26.333 --> 00:01:28.458
a place through a door,

23
00:01:28.458 --> 00:01:31.833
in the same way through these
tendencies the seeker

24
00:01:31.833 --> 00:01:35.750
is pulled toward inner destruction.

25
00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:38.000
Nashanam atmanah

26
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:39.833
does not mean the destruction of the soul,

27
00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:42.291
because the soul is indestructible.

28
00:01:42.291 --> 00:01:43.750
The indication here is

29
00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:47.291
that these tendencies corrupt the
direction of the soul.

30
00:01:47.291 --> 00:01:50.166
They take it away from truth and liberation,

31
00:01:50.166 --> 00:01:52.000
cover discernment,

32
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.583
and cloud remembrance.

33
00:01:54.583 --> 00:01:57.041
Now understand the inner connection
between them.

34
00:01:57.041 --> 00:02:01.416
Kamah is a craving for what you
do not yet have –

35
00:02:01.416 --> 00:02:03.666
the desire to obtain it.

36
00:02:03.666 --> 00:02:05.791
When this desire is not fulfilled,

37
00:02:05.791 --> 00:02:07.583
krodhah, anger, arises.

38
00:02:07.583 --> 00:02:10.583
And when it is fulfilled, that same satisfaction

39
00:02:10.583 --> 00:02:14.958
turns into lobhah, greed –
‘more, more, still more.’

40
00:02:14.958 --> 00:02:17.791
In this way they give birth to each other

41
00:02:17.791 --> 00:02:21.458
and bind the seeker in a cycle of suffering.

42
00:02:21.458 --> 00:02:24.375
This is why Lord Krishna commands –

43
00:02:24.375 --> 00:02:26.250
‘Tasmat tyajet’,

44
00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:28.333
therefore, give them up.

45
00:02:28.333 --> 00:02:30.541
This renunciation is not of outer objects,

46
00:02:30.541 --> 00:02:34.000
but of the inner attachment and stubbornness.

47
00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.875
This is the seeker's first step toward progress.

48
00:02:42.375 --> 00:02:43.666
I have given you

49
00:02:43.666 --> 00:02:46.875
a clear warning.

50
00:02:46.875 --> 00:02:50.791
There are three gateways to suffering.

51
00:02:50.791 --> 00:02:53.291
They do not open on their own.

52
00:02:53.291 --> 00:02:56.791
You open them, one by one.

53
00:02:56.791 --> 00:03:00.625
The desire you do not check

54
00:03:00.625 --> 00:03:03.208
becomes kamah,

55
00:03:03.208 --> 00:03:06.708
that is, lust.

56
00:03:06.708 --> 00:03:11.000
The reaction you leave unchecked

57
00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:14.958
becomes krodhah, anger.

58
00:03:14.958 --> 00:03:18.041
The gain you cling to

59
00:03:18.041 --> 00:03:21.416
becomes lobhah, greed.

60
00:03:21.416 --> 00:03:25.583
Slowly your peace begins to diminish.

61
00:03:25.583 --> 00:03:30.125
Lust burns your patience.

62
00:03:30.125 --> 00:03:34.083
Anger covers your discernment.

63
00:03:34.083 --> 00:03:40.000
Greed binds your freedom.

64
00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:45.208
In the beginning, this is not visible.

65
00:03:45.208 --> 00:03:48.666
But it changes –

66
00:03:48.666 --> 00:03:52.000
how you see others,

67
00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:58.416
how you speak, and how you treat yourself.

68
00:03:58.416 --> 00:04:01.666
But the truth is –

69
00:04:01.666 --> 00:04:05.166
the key is still in your hands.

70
00:04:05.166 --> 00:04:08.958
‘Tasmat tyajet.’

71
00:04:08.958 --> 00:04:12.541
Therefore, give them up.

72
00:04:12.541 --> 00:04:14.791
Not by force,

73
00:04:14.791 --> 00:04:17.333
but through awareness.

74
00:04:17.333 --> 00:04:19.583
Watch your mind.

75
00:04:19.583 --> 00:04:23.125
When desire arises, pause.

76
00:04:23.125 --> 00:04:26.041
When anger surges,

77
00:04:26.041 --> 00:04:28.166
breathe deeply

78
00:04:28.166 --> 00:04:32.208
and think before reacting.

79
00:04:32.208 --> 00:04:37.083
When greed tempts, question yourself.

80
00:04:37.083 --> 00:04:42.125
Closing the door in time is always easier.

81
00:04:42.125 --> 00:04:48.166
Getting out after being trapped within is hard.

82
00:04:48.166 --> 00:04:52.833
Renounce these three, and see,

83
00:04:52.833 --> 00:04:55.625
space and time both

84
00:04:55.625 --> 00:04:58.125
appear within,

85
00:04:58.125 --> 00:05:04.083
where your spiritual progress
begins to happen naturally.

86
00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:10.541
I have seen –

87
00:05:10.541 --> 00:05:13.458
a single harsh sentence

88
00:05:13.458 --> 00:05:16.208
spoken in a moment

89
00:05:16.208 --> 00:05:19.875
of anger can break years of trust.

90
00:05:19.875 --> 00:05:23.041
I have called krodhah

91
00:05:23.041 --> 00:05:26.916
one of the gateways to hell,

92
00:05:26.916 --> 00:05:32.083
because it does not only wound you.

93
00:05:32.083 --> 00:05:36.250
It burns those closest to you too.

94
00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:40.333
Relationships in the home are built slowly.

95
00:05:40.333 --> 00:05:43.916
Through time, care,

96
00:05:43.916 --> 00:05:48.208
shared memories, and sacrifice.

97
00:05:48.208 --> 00:05:51.833
But anger is impatient.

98
00:05:51.833 --> 00:05:55.375
It does not ask, it attacks.

99
00:05:55.375 --> 00:06:00.208
Words that come out in that heat
do not only sting.

100
00:06:00.208 --> 00:06:03.708
They stay in the heart.

101
00:06:03.708 --> 00:06:06.416
Even after the moment passes,

102
00:06:06.416 --> 00:06:11.208
they keep echoing in your loved ones' hearts.

103
00:06:11.208 --> 00:06:15.708
You may justify it.

104
00:06:15.708 --> 00:06:19.166
Saying ‘I was agitated,’

105
00:06:19.166 --> 00:06:20.791
or ‘they provoked me.’

106
00:06:20.791 --> 00:06:26.291
But think – that one moment,

107
00:06:26.291 --> 00:06:29.791
what did it truly take from you?

108
00:06:29.791 --> 00:06:33.083
If you truly care,

109
00:06:33.083 --> 00:06:37.750
pause before speaking in anger.

110
00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:41.541
Let love speak first.

111
00:06:41.541 --> 00:06:45.791
Stay in silence until clarity returns.

112
00:06:45.791 --> 00:06:48.500
That small gap between reaction

113
00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:56.166
and response – that is where
homes are preserved.

114
00:06:56.166 --> 00:06:57.583
Or else they break.

115
00:07:02.291 --> 00:07:03.958
I have said –

116
00:07:03.958 --> 00:07:07.375
kama, that is, lust, krodha,

117
00:07:07.375 --> 00:07:11.541
and lobha are gateways to hell,

118
00:07:11.541 --> 00:07:16.416
and they apply in your professional life too.

119
00:07:16.416 --> 00:07:21.041
Perhaps you use them as tools to advance.

120
00:07:21.041 --> 00:07:24.583
A deal driven by greed,

121
00:07:24.583 --> 00:07:28.041
a presentation sharpened by arrogance,

122
00:07:28.041 --> 00:07:32.333
or a decision forced through.

123
00:07:32.333 --> 00:07:37.500
From the outside this may look like progress.

124
00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:41.333
But what is the true cost?

125
00:07:41.333 --> 00:07:44.833
You lose peace of mind.

126
00:07:44.833 --> 00:07:47.333
You lose people's trust.

127
00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:51.375
You lose your true self, because

128
00:07:51.375 --> 00:07:55.666
slowly you begin to justify everything

129
00:07:55.666 --> 00:07:59.208
that takes you one step ahead.

130
00:07:59.208 --> 00:08:02.875
When greed grows, a person begins to reach

131
00:08:02.875 --> 00:08:05.958
for unjust means.

132
00:08:05.958 --> 00:08:10.708
The gain shines on the outside, but from within

133
00:08:10.708 --> 00:08:16.541
it destroys wealth, reputation, and peace alike.

134
00:08:16.541 --> 00:08:18.208
Remember,

135
00:08:18.208 --> 00:08:24.583
the higher you climb on the
wrong ladder, the harder the fall.

136
00:08:24.583 --> 00:08:28.875
A promotion gained through
deceit does not last.

137
00:08:28.875 --> 00:08:31.916
A team built on fear does not hold.

138
00:08:31.916 --> 00:08:37.250
Success without integrity does not satisfy.

139
00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:41.166
It only demands more.

140
00:08:41.166 --> 00:08:44.083
You are not made for a blind race.

141
00:08:44.083 --> 00:08:45.375
You are made to lead

142
00:08:45.375 --> 00:08:49.291
with clarity and values.

143
00:08:49.291 --> 00:08:53.750
So pause and ask –

144
00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:56.875
‘Which feeling is truly

145
00:08:56.875 --> 00:09:01.333
driving me right now?’

146
00:09:01.333 --> 00:09:05.000
If the answer is one of these three – lust,

147
00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:08.208
anger, or greed –

148
00:09:08.208 --> 00:09:11.041
take a step back,

149
00:09:11.041 --> 00:09:14.625
and anchor your life in sacred values

150
00:09:14.625 --> 00:09:18.250
and divine wisdom.

151
00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:20.416
Reflect on this.
